 stays grassy and pale. Black tea is fully oxidised, which gives it a darker colour and a malty taste.\n\nBrewing matters as much as the leaf. Green tea turns bitter in boiling water and does best at about 80\u00b0C for two minutes. Black tea needs a full boil and three to five minutes.\n\n<doc-file kind=\"other\" filename=\".drafts/demo.md\" title=\"Demo\">\n\n<user-attention low>\nHerbal infusions such as peppermint, chamomile and rooibos contain no tea leaf, so they are strictly tisanes and have no caffeine.", "ttft_ms": 3666, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 7636, "uuid": "84f4a086-dd73-48e7-8010-20ae6f4bfc75", "ttft_stream_ms": 2215, "time_to_request_ms": 122, "first_content_frame_ms": 2216, "queued_turn_count": 0, "result_index": 0}
